  <h2>How to Save on Your Next MRI</h2>

  <h3>Ask the right questions:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      What’s the total cost of this MRI, including the radiologist fee and
      contrast?
    </li>
    <li>Is this price the same with or without insurance?</li>
    <li>Can I get that quote in writing?</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Compare facilities:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Look for <strong>ACR-accredited centers</strong></li>
    <li>Ask about machine specs: <strong>1.5T or 3T MRI</strong> is ideal</li>
    <li>Confirm radiologist credentials: <strong>Board-certified</strong></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Watch for red flags:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>“We can’t quote a price until after the scan”</li>
    <li>“Radiologist billing is separate”</li>
    <li>“Contrast is not included in the quote”</li>
  </ul>

